{
  "_doc": "The atmosphere (view only, #411): how the world's light and air look, laid over the frame by one pass (src/view/atmosphere.lobster). A mood's knobs: exposure, contrast, saturation (-1 to 1, 0 leaves it); shadow_tint and highlight_tint, colours the dark and the bright parts lean to, by shadow and highlight (0 to 1); haze_colour laid over the view by haze (0 to 1), thickest toward the top of the screen from haze_start (0 the bottom, 1 the top) and drifting by haze_drift (0 to 1); vignette (0 to 1) darkens the corners from vignette_radius (0 to 2); bloom (0 to 2) adds a soft blur of what is brighter than bloom_threshold (0 to 1); glow (0 to 4) is how much the glows light what is round them, glow_air (0 to 1) how much they light the air. A mood of all zeros draws the frame as it is. default is the mood a map gets unless maps names its own; atmosphere:<mood> picks one, atmosphere:off none. glows: the lights the game places (building_fire, ruin_fire, window, flash, shot), each a colour (or \"own\": the thing's own), a radius in canvas px, a strength (0 to 4) and a flicker (0 to 1); a source left out doesn't glow. A mod's atmosphere.json merges over this; a mood can start from another with \"extends\".",
